# Experiment sweep output (staged models + solver output + report). Reproducible
# from run_experiments.py, so it is never tracked. Since 2026-09-03 it is a SYMLINK to
# /scratch/tpj8/nj_bight_sfincs/experiments (1 TB tier, NOT backed up, purged when idle);
# the target must stay writable and outside the read-only archive (tests/test_repo_hygiene).
# No trailing slash: a `dir/` pattern does not match a symlink.
experiments

# Data. Ignored wholesale, then the small SOURCE files are un-ignored below.
# The domain definitions — the catalog, the region polygons, the refinement
# polygons, the flux cross-sections — ARE SOURCE. Only the rasters they point at
# are bulk. In the pre-2026-08 repos the whole of data/ was untracked, which put
# the three files that actually define a domain outside version control.
data/*
!data/*/
data/*/*
!data/data_catalog.yml
!data/region_*.geojson
!data/quadtree/*.geojson
!data/flux_crosssections.geojson
!data/flux_crosssections.crs
!data/roughness/*.csv
!data/buildings_*/manifest.json
!data/roughness/*.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Logs
*.log
logs/
# ...but keep the directory itself: hpc/*.slurm write to logs/ via `#SBATCH -e
# logs/<job>.out`, and sbatch fails outright if the directory is absent in a fresh clone.
!logs/.gitkeep

# reports/ holds scored CSVs, which ARE tracked; the figure/animation bulk is not.
reports/figures/
reports/**/animations/

# Toolchain — symlinks into ~/nj_sandy_sfincs (see CLAUDE.md). No trailing slash:
# a `dir/` pattern does not match a symlink, so the trailing-slash form would leave
# these showing as untracked forever.
micromamba
hydromt_sfincs
*.sif
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# Jupyter checkpoints (there is no notebooks/ dir yet, but the pattern is free)
.ipynb_checkpoints/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ⚠️ .gitignore DOES NOT IGNORE ITSELF. The previous repo carried a bare
# `.gitignore` line here, so a fresh clone got no ignore rules at all and every
# staged model, raster and log showed up as untracked. Do not re-add it.

# Papers — symlinked into the read-only archive (docs, not code). See ARCHIVE.md.
refs
